WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO is about to start!

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:11.440
Kidokawa Seishuu makes impressive passes and keeps the ball in possession!

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:08.760
Izumi!

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:11.440
Ooisokawa!

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.000
What's going on here?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.320
I thought they were fighting amongst themselves!

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.030
<i>Defeat Raimon!</i>

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.070
<i>Win and you'll be able to see the path you should continue on!</i>

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.210
Kishibe heads up!

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.190
He got past Raimon!

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:31.710
Sousuke!

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.950
Kidokawa Seishuu makes a pass!

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.450
He's completely free!

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:38.610
Sangoku-san!

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.140
It's ours!

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:45.690
What?!

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.540
There it is! Water World Stadium's pitch-down!

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.780
It's been forever since I last saw you, Japan.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:06.490
Raimon is saved by the pitch-down!

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:09.480
Water World Stadium has what's called the pitch-down system,

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:13.950
where the field will either drop horizontally or vertically into the water for a given amount of time!

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:19.000
Where and when it drops is random, making it impossible to predict!

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:21.780
I can't believe it was set up like this...

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:22.470
Yeah...

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:25.260
Kidokawa wasn't told about it?

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.710
Aphrodi.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.150
About the next stadium...

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.210
There's no need to tell me.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:38.790
I want to fight under the same conditions as Raimon.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.160
Pitch-down...

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.370
First, we'll have to figure out how to work with it...

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.550
<i>You're not getting past us!</i>

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.550
I could've stopped him.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:09.580
The match resumes with Raimon in possession of the ball!

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:15.060
Whenever the ball is dropped in Water World Stadium, it goes to the other team for a free kick!

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.350
Tenma!

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.620
Don't get scared by how this stadium is set up!

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.900
Jump over it like a bunny rabbit!

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:31.120
The third match in Holy Road's Nationals tournament,
 Raimon versus Kidokawa Seishuu, is in its first half at 0-0!

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.800
Will it be Raimon or Kidokawa Seishuu to score first?!

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:36.960
Shindou!

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:38.340
Fight me!

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.030
Presto Turn!

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.260
You've gotten better!

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:51.970
Tenma!

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.390
Another pitch-down!

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:06.540
Both teams keep getting stopped by the pitch-down and are unable to fully attack!

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:10.950
It's no use. I can't form a strategy out of this.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:15.400
Should I separate the offense from defense to cover ground?

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:20.590
But if our opponent were to rush in to attack, we won't have enough people to defend...

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.210
Tobisawa!

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.700
Kidokawa Seishuu gets through!

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:25.940
Not on my watch!

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.140
But Raimon skillfully avoids this with a touch!

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:34.350
Kishibe!

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:43.570
Has he found a way through it?

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:49.530
With their abilities, they'll be able to cope with it.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.830
The match resumes with Kidokawa Seishuu's throw-in!

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:58.580
What do they have in mind?

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:01.330
Izumi!

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:02.000
Tobisawa!

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.510
Hissatsu tactics!

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.250
God Triangle!

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.310
God Triangle?

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:13.360
Now, Kidokawa Seishuu has made their move!

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:14.820
But here comes a pitch-down!

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:16.280
Izumi!

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:17.770
What?!

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:18.940
They dodge it!

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:28.990
Kidokawa Seishuu cleverly dodges the pitch-down and makes their way up!

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:32.370
I see...

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.700
See what?

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:40.440
God Triangle is a triangle formation that moves up in tandem by dribbling.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:44.630
In this way, they're able to proactively react against the pitch-down, no matter where it occurs.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:50.780
Kidokawa Seishuu's ability to make instantaneous decisions, as well as the technique to uphold them,

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:49.760
Tobisawa!

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:52.760
are what makes this hissatsu tactics achievable for them.

00:06:55.130 --> 00:07:01.140
During the short time he became Kidokawa Seishuu's coach, he's gained an accurate grasp of his players' abilities...

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:04.010
He's even put God Triangle to practical use on this field,

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:09.280
a hissatsu tactics that he most surely came up with in order to increase their breakthrough offense...

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:11.450
That's it! Go!

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.450
They get past Kirino!

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.410
Look out!

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.410
Dash Train!

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:30.080
Kurumada stops him with his hissatsu technique!

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:34.700
But Kidokawa's fierce offense won't stop!

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:36.220
I'll stop you!

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.100
Illusion Ball!

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:45.370
Raimon's defense is broken through again!

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:50.800
Sangoku just barely manages to block the ball!

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.640
Why aren't you using me?

00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:59.790
With this, we can win.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.780
These inadequates are trying to lead a revolution? Don't make me laugh.

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.720
If this keeps up, we'll lose.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:12.160
Coach, isn't there something we can do?

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:18.050
Here's the place.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:19.170
Kamiya!

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:22.430
Kidokawa Seishuu makes a wide centering!

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:24.140
I won't let you have it!

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:27.310
Shinsuke!

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:29.770
That move...

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:41.040
Kidokawa Seishuu is stopped by the pitch-down!

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:43.500
Shindou!

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.170
Here it comes.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:55.420
Are they going to make their move?

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.850
The match resumes with Raimon's goal kick!

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:02.430
Let's go!

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.390
Hissatsu tactics! Flying Route Pass!

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.270
Flying Route Pass?

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:11.230
What are they up to?

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.230
Kirino!

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.170
Kurumada-san!

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.780
Raimon counterattacks this time!

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.950
Their passes are connecting!

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:25.210
What's going on?

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:30.240
Nishiki-senpai!

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.130
Yeah!

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:32.400
This is...!

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.310
I see...

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:35.700
So that's your game plan.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:40.840
Raimon isn't jumping after eyeing someone's passes.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.810
They're making their passes to the person who's jumped.

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:47.560
And they're making their passes before they land.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:52.400
By making passes mid-air, they are unaffected by the pitch-down.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:54.830
Captain!

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:59.280
What's more, our single formation is made up of three people.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:01.340
They have no trouble finding a course to send their passes.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:08.620
Your brain is still as sharp as ever, genius playmaker Kidou Yuuto.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.210
Shinsuke-kun!

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:15.120
Kirino-senpai!

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:16.590
Hamano!

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:19.040
This could do the trick!

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.600
Don't let your guard down just yet.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:25.200
Mark #9 and #10!

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.020
Huh?

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:31.520
He's landed!

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:32.770
Now!

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:35.030
Hamano!

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:39.810
Surfing Pierrot!

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:46.560
Hamano-senpai!

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.050
There!

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.750
Raimon's pass is cut!

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:54.520
Sousuke!

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:58.720
I'm more than enough for these guys.

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:11.100
Iron Horse Warrior Knight!

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:12.690
An Avatar!

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:15.900
He can use an Avatar!

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:23.360
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:28.150
This is...

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.160
Tsurugi, teach me how to play the card game!

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:32.450
All right.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:35.140
I strengthen my characters with my Coach card!

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:36.910
Incredible...

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:38.900
But how about this?!

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.480
As expected of you, Captain.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.250
Sword Saint Lancelot!

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:47.530
I won't lose! Instrumentalist Maestro!

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:49.090
I'll be the one to win!

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:50.400
You still have far to go.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:52.880
Inazuma Eleven GO card game!

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.920
We'll be waiting for you at the movies!

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:59.270
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:13.270
Gallop Buster!

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.170
Fence Of Gaia!

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:27.890
Goal!

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:29.880
The balance has finally been tipped!

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:33.020
Kidokawa Seishuu makes the first goal!

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:47.500
Sousuke, that was a bit-

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.710
Sorry, sorry.

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:50.890
But I had to grab my chance.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:56.710
It's still one point!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.040
Let's go redeem ourselves!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:58.790
Yeah!

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:04.030
Kidokawa Seishuu appears to be gathering strength from their goal because they keep their offense!

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:09.830
I'll stop you!

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:12.600
But Raimon isn't giving up!

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.250
Everyone's marked.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:20.180
In that case...

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.390
It's mine!

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:28.430
Nishiki gets the ball stolen from him this time!

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:33.230
Sousuke!

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:36.060
I won't let you!

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:40.640
Hunter's Net!

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:48.380
We're not done yet!

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:51.680
Let's go!

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:52.820
Yeah!

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:04.850
Triangle ZZ!

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.430
Goal!

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:11.720
Kidokawa Seishuu makes another goal!

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:15.760
There's the whistle ending the first half!

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:18.680
We'll meet the second half with a score of 2-0!

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:25.980
All right, it's half-time.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.780
Kidokawa sure is strong...

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:35.310
Everyone, make sure you're rehydrated.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:38.240
I'm sorry. I wasn't able to defend the goal.

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:39.570
Don't worry about it.

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:42.700
The minute they've brought it to the goalkeeper, it's our fault.

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:51.890
Nii-san, what happened to teamwork?!

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:55.150
I made the goal, didn't I?

00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:56.210
Outta my way.

00:14:58.570 --> 00:14:59.490
Coach.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:04.030
Maybe it's a good idea to take Sousuke off for the second half.

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:08.090
I feel that if he stays on, he'll upset the temporary truce that our team has with each other.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:10.140
No, I'm keeping him on.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:12.040
But at this rate...

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:14.700
Don't underestimate Raimon.

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:21.160
Driving them deeper and deeper into a corner only makes them bring out new power that evolves them further.

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:23.750
That is Raimon's soccer.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:28.820
And that soccer is still inherited by them to this day.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:32.760
We will need Sousuke's abilities in this match.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:35.480
But Coach...

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:39.060
Besides, a victory is meaningful when everyone on the team is involved.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:45.540
What's more, by winning a victory of real merit, you will see the path you are meant to take.

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:49.530
The path that we're meant to take...

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:53.770
Yes, sir.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.670
If only I'd made the shoot back then...

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:15.050
In any case, we'll have to keep moving around to get their mark off us.

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:16.350
Yeah...

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:18.380
Who's that?

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:20.560
No idea...

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:22.670
Nishiki.

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:24.780
M-Master!

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:26.650
Master?

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.170
It's been a while, Kidou.

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:34.010
Someoka!

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:35.450
Someoka-san!

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:37.110
Someoka?

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:41.900
S-Someoka-san?! You mean, from the legendary Raimon Eleven?!

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:43.930
Yeah, that's right.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:46.700
I'm gonna borrow this.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.420
You're drawing on the ball?

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:53.810
What are you doing?

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:55.280
All done.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:56.860
Nishiki!

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:01.620
Let's see now...

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:02.910
Aim for that tree.

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:16.830
Looks like you've completed that training I told you to do.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:21.080
The training he told him to do?

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:36.150
Someoka is playing for a pro league team in Italy...

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:37.520
So that's how it is.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:38.970
Nishiki.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.070
You'll be fine.

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:44.120
All you're missing now...

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.530
...is food!

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:47.930
Yes, sir!

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:52.430
Master's onigiri is the best thing ever!

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:54.330
Oh, really!

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:56.790
Hey, chew before you swallow!

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:59.790
Weirdos.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:02.720
I'm changing our positions for the second half!

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.350
We're about to begin the second half!

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:10.400
The score is 2-0 with Kidokawa Seishuu in the lead!

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.540
Will Raimon catch up?!

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:16.200
Raimon has made changes to their positions!

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:22.920
Their forward Tsurugi is put back as midfielder, while their midfielder Nishiki is moved up as a forward!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.760
Why won't he use me?

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:31.450
Is #10 going to come at us with a middle shoot?

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.490
There's the kickoff!

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:40.160
Sousuke, pass it to me!

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:42.330
This will end it!

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.290
Tsurugi steals the ball!

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:46.460
What?!

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:48.620
Don't get too cocky.

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:52.380
Don't let him shoot!

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:00.090
#10 is a decoy?

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:01.810
Nishiki-senpai is free!

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:05.410
Here is my samurai spirit!

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:15.060
Sengoku War God Musashi!

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:19.130
He can use an Avatar?!

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.140
Here I go!

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:34.880
Goal!

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:37.290
Nishiki's Avatar shoot goes in!

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:39.710
Raimon takes back one point!

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:41.490
All right!

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.140
Good one, Nishiki!

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:47.090
Nishiki-senpai!

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:48.070
Nishiki!

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:50.130
When did you gain that skill?

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:52.600
It's all thanks to my teacher.

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:54.670
That old man?

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:59.630
He's had the ability to bring out an Avatar since a long time ago.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:04.750
But what he needed was self-confidence, to believe that he could do it too.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.050
And that's why you gave him that training?

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:08.240
Yeah.

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:13.460
It didn't matter what it was. As long as he could accomplish one thing, it'll strengthen his confidence.

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:18.910
All that was left after that was to make him eat so he can relax and demonstrate his real abilities.

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:23.040
All right, one more point to go!

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:23.850
Let's catch up!

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:24.920
Yeah!

00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:29.140
As if I'll let that happen!

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:32.750
Kidokawa Seishuu's Taki Sousuke heads up!

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:35.900
But he runs into a pitch-down!

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:41.630
Hunter's Net!

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:47.080
Tenma-kun!

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:50.830
I won't let you!

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:53.120
Soyokaze Step!

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:58.810
Nishiki-senpai!

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:08.670
Sengoku War God Musashi!

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:09.910
Katayama!

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:14.010
You got past me before, but not this time!

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:21.080
Heavy Machine Soldier Baron!

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:34.220
Goal!

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:37.040
Raimon makes a tie at last!

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:39.630
The game is back with both teams on even footing!

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:41.430
All right!

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:53.190
Now this is the Raimon I know.

00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:40.890
Nishiki-senpai awakens at last!

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:43.080
Look upon his Raimon spirit!

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:48.540
Next on Inazuma Eleven GO, 
 Avatar! The Arrival Of Sengoku War God Musashi!!

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:50.640
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:24:00.050 --> 00:24:02.780
The Inazuma Eleven GO's proverb today is...

00:24:08.060 --> 00:24:11.670
All you're missing now, is food!

00:24:11.670 --> 00:24:12.620
That's all!
